desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Avoid Default Routes"
	title_zh: "Avoid Default Routes"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-avoid-default-routes"
	risk: "security-misconfiguration"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `avoid-default-routes` (ruby/rails/security/audit/xss/avoid-default-routes.yaml).
Original message: Default routes are enabled in this routes file. This means any public method on a controller can be called as an action. It is very easy to accidentally expose a method you didn't mean to. Instead, remove this line and explicitly include all routes you intend external users to follow.
CWE: CWE-276: Incorrect Default Permissions
References:
- https://github.com/presidentbeef/brakeman/blob/main/docs/warning_types/default_routes/index.markdown
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
Original paths.include: ['*routes.rb'].
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://routes.rb": <<<POS
map.connect ":controller/:action/:id"
POS
	"safefile://routes.rb": <<<NEG
root 'home#index'
NEG
)

${*routes.rb}.pattern_regex(/(?:map\.connect\s+":controller\/:action\/:id")|(?:match\s+':controller\(\/:action\(\/:id\(\.:format\)\)\)')/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Avoid Default Routes",
	title_zh: "Avoid Default Routes",
	message: "Avoid Default Routes detected.",
}
